title: Cloudflare Status API Checker
agents: special_agent
catalog: tbd
license: GPL
distribution: github
description:
 Monitor the Cloudflare Services through their public API.
 By default one service per group is discovered (e.g. "Europe",
 "Cloudflare Sites and Services"), with individual datacenters or
 components listed only in the group service's details.
 Status will be checked and OK for operational, WARN for
 degraded performance, partial outages or planned maintenance,
 and CRIT for major outages or any other unidentified state.
 A group service's details only list its non-operational
 subcomponents (plus an "N/M operational" count) to avoid
 exceeding Checkmk's long-output size limit.

 The "Cloudflare Status API discovery" ruleset controls this:
 with "Grouping enabled" (the default) only the groups are
 discovered. With "Grouping disabled", a name filter is shown -
 every API component (group or leaf) whose name contains one of
 the given strings (case-insensitive) is discovered as its own
 service; leave the filter empty to discover every component
 individually. A bare 3-letter airport code can match unrelated
 words (e.g. "fra" also matches "France"), so include the
 parentheses (e.g. "(FRA)") or use the full city name.

inventory:
 One item per service discovered, as controlled by the
 "Cloudflare Status API discovery" ruleset (see above).
